(1853876, 254015, 47487, '<td valign="top">it''s a bummer how hard it is to capture a good reflection without completely blowing out the sky. Great effort here, though -- the bottom two-thirds of the image is just gorgeous.</td>', 'it''s a bummer how hard it is to capture a good reflection without completely blowing out the sky. Great effort here, though -- the bottom two-thirds of the image is just gorgeous.', '2005-11-10 03:57:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1853879, 255450, 47487, '<td valign="top">well-composed. Very pretty.</td>', 'well-composed. Very pretty.', '2005-11-10 03:57:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1853885, 253682, 45857, '<td valign="top">A very good image, except for one disturbing effect, which I''m not sure how to correct. To me it appears the river flows uphill, especially in the left side of the frame.<br/>(Ah! got it....the horizon line should be the vanishing points of the water, the two places where the water merges with the hills. If you draw a line between the two points, then rotate the image until the line is parallel with the bottom of the frame, it will work. A small level on your tripod head might help.)</td>', 'A very good image, except for one disturbing effect, which I''m not sure how to correct. To me it appears the river flows uphill, especially in the left side of the frame.(Ah! got it....the horizon line should be the vanishing points of the water, the two places where the water merges with the hills. If you draw a line between the two points, then rotate the image until the line is parallel with the bottom of the frame, it will work. A small level on your tripod head might help.)', '2005-11-10 04:07:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1853887, 255272, 45857, '<td valign="top">Got to watch your compostion, the guy wire hurts.</td>', 'Got to watch your compostion, the guy wire hurts.', '2005-11-10 04:10:02.000000', NULL, 1),
