(1870928, 254922, 40718, '<td valign="top">Congrats Alan, this really is a great shot of Pittsburgh.</td>', 'Congrats Alan, this really is a great shot of Pittsburgh.', '2005-11-16 00:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1870929, 255472, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ubique:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice to see a really high quality landscape in a ''portrait'' format.  This is a very fine composition; lovely lines &amp; proportions.  Beautiful colours and light ... spectacular but not strident.  Also some interesting textural contrasts.  All things considered, it''s an image that is so unpresumptuous at first glance that it might be easy to overlook just how effortless and harmonious it actually is.  I hope it isn''t overlooked in favour of more flashy models!</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I guess it was :-) Though 6.4 and 30th ain''t bad... I was definitely conscious of wanting to do a portrait orientationt his time, and I was definitely conscious that I''m getting typecast for technicolor, so I went more muted. I bet if I had brightened this up it would have scored better, but this is a pretty straight rendition of the scene, a relatively rare thing for me. I like to play with colors and saturation on these shots as a rule, it pleases me.<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the kind comments people :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by ubique: Nice to see a really high quality landscape in a ''portrait'' format.  This is a very fine composition; lovely lines & proportions.  Beautiful colours and light ... spectacular but not strident.  Also some interesting textural contrasts.  All things considered, it''s an image that is so unpresumptuous at first glance that it might be easy to overlook just how effortless and harmonious it actually is.  I hope it isn''t overlooked in favour of more flashy models!  I guess it was :-) Though 6.4 and 30th ain''t bad... I was definitely conscious of wanting to do a portrait orientationt his time, and I was definitely conscious that I''m getting typecast for technicolor, so I went more muted. I bet if I had brightened this up it would have scored better, but this is a pretty straight rendition of the scene, a relatively rare thing for me. I like to play with colors and saturation on these shots as a rule, it pleases me. Thanks for all the kind comments people :-)', '2005-11-16 00:26:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1870938, 255504, 14620, '<td valign="top">Yet another great 6+ image.  Thanks for showing me this place.  And not one comment about them being the same place. :-)</td>', 'Yet another great 6+ image.  Thanks for showing me this place.  And not one comment about them being the same place. :-)', '2005-11-16 00:27:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1870943, 253891, 40718, '<td valign="top">This was an awesome shot!  I guess I forgot it''s Natural BRIDGE instead of Arch.</td>', 'This was an awesome shot!  I guess I forgot it''s Natural BRIDGE instead of Arch.', '2005-11-16 00:28:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1870958, 255402, 37393, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Mary Ann Melton:</b></div><hr/><i> When I think of landscape - I think of an intimate setting in the woods or by a stream, or a wide vista with mountains.  I voted this one lower because I did not feel it met the challenge very well. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I understand that my photo isn''t great.. but just because it doesn''t fall within a narrow definition of a landscape, does not mean that it didn''t meet the challenge. The challenge was to provide the viewer with a refreshing landscape shot; to me this meant to think outside the landscape box..and not just take a picture of a stream in the woods, etc.</td>', 'Originally posted by Mary Ann Melton: When I think of landscape - I think of an intimate setting in the woods or by a stream, or a wide vista with mountains.  I voted this one lower because I did not feel it met the challenge very well.   I understand that my photo isn''t great.. but just because it doesn''t fall within a narrow definition of a landscape, does not mean that it didn''t meet the challenge. The challenge was to provide the viewer with a refreshing landscape shot; to me this meant to think outside the landscape box..and not just take a picture of a stream in the woods, etc.', '2005-11-16 00:31:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1870967, 255412, 36956, '<td valign="top">haha.  Great shot.  I have shot that exact spot numerous times with my freind zoomdak.  We still have dibs on it when we return from college.  great work!<br/> <br/>mH</td>', 'haha.  Great shot.  I have shot that exact spot numerous times with my freind zoomdak.  We still have dibs on it when we return from college.  great work! mH', '2005-11-16 00:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1870969, 255464, 39429, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot and nice finish.  Welcome to the site.  We have some awesome Utah members.  I love this mountain.<br/>Becky</td>', 'Wonderful shot and nice finish.  Welcome to the site.  We have some awesome Utah members.  I love this mountain.Becky', '2005-11-16 00:33:20.000000', NULL, 0),
