(1872215, 255115, 18148, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your comments, they were very helpful. This was my first challenge entry and I learned a lot. I did go back and tweak the levels, contrast and brightness and it made a huge difference. I wasn''t sure how much Basic Editing allowed me to tweak the picture so I left the it pretty much as it came from the camera.<br/>Again everyone thanks for your comments.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for your comments, they were very helpful. This was my first challenge entry and I learned a lot. I did go back and tweak the levels, contrast and brightness and it made a huge difference. I wasn''t sure how much Basic Editing allowed me to tweak the picture so I left the it pretty much as it came from the camera.Again everyone thanks for your comments.', '2005-11-16 09:14:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1872246, 255288, 42574, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Dad on an impressive finish for your first time!</td>', 'Congratulations Dad on an impressive finish for your first time!', '2005-11-16 09:26:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1872258, 255182, 36283, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mcrochip:</b></div><hr/><i> Is that a distant bird, or a spot of dirt on your lense.. just below the center of the shot.  Smalll distraction on an otherwise nice shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are right.. that is a distant bird. I had seen that too</td>', 'Originally posted by mcrochip: Is that a distant bird, or a spot of dirt on your lense.. just below the center of the shot.  Smalll distraction on an otherwise nice shot.   You are right.. that is a distant bird. I had seen that too', '2005-11-16 09:30:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1872272, 255577, 19178, '<td valign="top">Neil,<br/>Congratulations on a great finish.  The little figure in the image really sets it apart showing the "immensity of nature" -- like the style in Hudson River School paintings!</td>', 'Neil,Congratulations on a great finish.  The little figure in the image really sets it apart showing the "immensity of nature" -- like the style in Hudson River School paintings!', '2005-11-16 09:34:29.000000', NULL, 0),
