(1876402, 255620, 39664, '<td valign="top">Ok, now I have camera envy!  <br/> <br/>I don''t think you needed to use a 30 second shutter speed and if you really REALLY wanted to use that long of a shutter speed, I would have backed the ISO down to 100 or 200.  Also, switching to manual focus and setting your focus prior to clicking the shutter would have made this more sharp.  <br/> <br/>I took my all time best shot at night using those settings, if you care to take a look.  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=251000" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/399/thumb/251000.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/399/thumb/251000.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/399/thumb/251000.jpg"/></a> <br/>But hey, I didn''t finish much higher than you in this challenge so I hope my "advice" is taken in the spirit of which it is intended!  :-p</td>', 'Ok, now I have camera envy!   I don''t think you needed to use a 30 second shutter speed and if you really REALLY wanted to use that long of a shutter speed, I would have backed the ISO down to 100 or 200.  Also, switching to manual focus and setting your focus prior to clicking the shutter would have made this more sharp.   I took my all time best shot at night using those settings, if you care to take a look.   But hey, I didn''t finish much higher than you in this challenge so I hope my "advice" is taken in the spirit of which it is intended!  :-p', '2005-11-17 08:01:28.000000', NULL, 0),
